summary:
Proves the Cohen–Lenstra–Martinet conjecture (1.1) for p = 3 and G any transitive permutation 2-group with a transposition (for example D₄): the average of |Cl_K[3]| over G-extensions of any number field tends to an explicit constant (Theorems 1.1, 6.1), about 1.42 for D₄-quartics over ℚ. It also proves that the relative class group average is 1 + 3^{−u}, as the heuristics predict (Theorems 1.2, 6.11), and treats C₂ ≀ H more generally (Theorem 8.1). The strategy sums Datskovsky–Wright's average over quadratic extensions K/F of each index-2 subfield F. That needs a tail estimate uniform in F (Theorem 5.1), built from four ingredients:
- uniform counts of S₃ cubics and of h₃ over quadratic extensions (Theorem 3.1), using class field theory, the Shintani zeta function, and a new "propagation of orders" argument;
- a relative Ellenberg–Venkatesh lemma (Lemma 2.1);
- log-free zero-density estimates giving small split primes (§4);
- an induction on the tower.
The atlas plans Shintani zeta functions (AN.8), Hecke L-function basics (AN.4) and Shafarevich's theorem (IG.4), and Mathlib has class numbers, regulators and the unit theorem. It has none of the torsion, counting or average theorems. Six source issues are recorded, including a gap in the proof of Lemma 2.1 with an easy repair and a misprinted constant C_G. The D₄ table of Example 7.2 was reproduced numerically.
